From 91419a7e9bc9c8ad70e93a35979942fe1e9a6971 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: A9 project <dmayala@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 11:35:05 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] drm/a9_eink: control template in bytes 1..3 of every
 transport word

Boot 12 (E5c, first non-zero drive): the glass did not change. Stock drive
words carry the panel's control signals in bytes 1..3 (byte 1 gate clocks
and per-word source strobes, byte 2 0x00, byte 3 0xff): a fixed CONTROL
TEMPLATE that stock builds once at TCON start (composer
HWCDisplay::SetPowerMode, librecovery_ui.so Init_Eink_SWTcon) and never
overwrites; byte 0 is the 2-bit drive data. The transport zero-filled
bytes 1..3, so the gate/source drivers were never clocked. MEASURED: 16
live stock ring buffers equal the template in bytes 1..3 on all 371,392
words; one buffer per set equals it entirely (stock's idle frame).

- request_firmware("hisense/a9-ctrl-template.bin"): 80-byte header +
  one frame, made from the user's own composer by a host tool (vendor
  data, never in the source). Accepted only if the header is exact, the
  payload SHA-256 equals the header's AND the compiled-in A9E_CT_SHA256
  (a88ae8ef...), and every word has byte 0 = 0, byte 2 = 0, byte 3 = 0xff
  (a9e_ct_check). Without it no update runs (dry or real) and the
  transport refuses to power up (-ENODATA).
- Both transport buffers hold the template from attach on. A frame is
  composed in one pass as (frame & byte-0 lanes) | template, so bytes
  1..3 always come from the validated template; the null decision is made
  on the byte 0 that went into the buffer (frame-progress interlock
  semantics unchanged). Every "zero" frame (power-on idle refreshes,
  power-off and blank, zero_test) is now the template itself (byte 0 =
  0): stock's idle frame, gates scanning, nothing driven.
- a9tcon core: the null frames of a table pass clear byte 0 only
  (clear_codes) instead of memset, as stock; the staging frame and the
  hold cache carry the template.
- transport_format: XR24 only (stock BA24 = data on the B lane, control
  on G = XRGB8888's layout, MEASURED); XB24 refused at probe.
- status line 1: " template %d"; zero test log: "template frames".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
